    "diagnosis": "Cutaneous mastocytosis",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Mastocytosis in the skin in an adult with the clinical picture of cutaneous mastocytosis (monomorphic maculopapular cutaneous mastocytosis). Immunohistochemistry for tryptase shows a moderate increase in mostly spindle-shaped mast cells. Only a few neoplastic mast cells show an aberrant expression of CD25 (not pictured). A bone marrow biopsy is indicated in this situation, because more than 90% of adult patients with the preliminary diagnosis of mastocytosis in the skin have systemic mastocytosis, usually indolent systemic mastocytosis.",
    "source": "",
